<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for <span class="icontiny" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warlock.gif");'></span>
<span class="c9">Destruction Warlock</span> DPS in Cataclysm Classic Pre-Raid. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from dungeons, professions, BoE World drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best In Slot Gear for Destruction Warlock DPS in Pre-Raid</h2>When gearing, there are a multitude of different things to consider; different talent specializations, your currently equipped gear, and your raid composition all play a key part. The biggest deciding factor of them all is Hit rating - having too much or too little Hit rating from either talents, gems, or buffs will result in you swapping in different pieces of gear or gems to reach the relevant Hit cap.<div class="box" data-level="null" style="display: block;">
<ul class="first">
<li class="fa fa-check">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Gearing Goals:</b></div></li>
<ol class="last">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Use the highest item level items in every slot to increase our <b>Intellect</b>, and <b>Secondary Stats</b>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Hit cap</b> is determined by the level of the target, with level 88 raid bosses requiring +17% chance to Hit, while level 87 trash mobs require only +6%. You should typically gear for bosses, but having a specialized setup for clearing trash may be worthwhile.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Soft Haste Cap</b> are different haste levels at which different of our damage over time abilities gain an extra tick of damage. It can be worthwhile to reach said caps if you are close to them and reforge any leftover haste. See the Attribute guide for the specific haste caps depending on spell and race.</div></li></ol></ul>
<div class="pad"></div>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
<table class="grid" style="width: 75%; max-width: 100%;">
<tbody>
<tr>
<td data-background="c9" style="width: 60%; max-width: 100%;">
<b>Hit Rating Caps</b></td>
<td data-background="c9" style="width: 10%; max-width: 100%;">
<b>Level 88</b></td>
<td data-background="c9" style="width: 10%; max-width: 100%;">
<b>Level 87</b></td>
<td data-background="c9" style="width: 10%; max-width: 100%;">
<b>Level 86</b></td>
<td data-background="c9" style="width: 10%; max-width: 100%;">
<b>Level 85</b></td></tr>
<tr>
<td data-background="c9">Hit Percent</td>
<td data-background="c9">17%</td>
<td data-background="c9">6%</td>
<td data-background="c9">5%</td>
<td data-background="c9">4%</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>Hit Rating</td>
<td>1742</td>
<td>615</td>
<td>512</td>
<td>410</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div>
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<ul class="last">
<li class="fa fa-warning">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<i>The recommendations listed below for each gear slot are simply that - <b>recommendations</b>. Chosen based on a combination of Mastery /<wbr/> Haste /<wbr/> Crit /<wbr/> Hit /<wbr/> Intellect, we have taken care to provide a range of alternatives.</i></div></li></ul></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="justice-points">Justice Points</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> are the Cataclysm version of <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=101/emblem-of-heroism">
<span>
<img alt="Emblem of Heroism" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_proclaimchampion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Heroism</span></span></a>, which means that they can be obtained by killing bosses in Heroic Dungeons and completing Random Dungeons through the Random Dungeon Finder tool. The main vendors you can exchange these at to obtain gear are <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=46555/gunra">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Gunra</span></a> for the Horde and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=44246/magatha-silverton">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Magatha Silverton</span></a> for the Alliance.<br/>
<br/>The order you purchase items here is heavily dependent on your luck. None of the items available for <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> are the best option in the slot, so grab what you think will be upgraded last. Overall getting Tier pieces first is a good idea<br/>
