<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="gems">Gems</h4>Red, purple, and orange gems are the best for Warlocks. Warlocks will often ignore the color if the bonus is not big enough. Instead, we should fill it with a red intellect gem. Warlocks only want to use orange or purple gems to gain a powerful socket bonus or meet our hit cap. Typically, Warlocks will change their gems to gain or lose hit or haste rating. We do this to meet specific hit or haste rating caps.<br/>
<br/>Whether you want to go for a socket bonus over pure red gems will depend on the size of the bonus. A good rule is: if the socket bonus is under 20 Int or 30 of any rating stat, ignore it and gem red. Of course, this depends on your gear and stats. It would be best to <a href="https://wowsims.github.io/cata/" target="_blank">simulate</a> your character to find the best solution.<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Meta Socket - <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=68780/burning-shadowspirit-diamond">
<img alt="Burning Shadowspirit Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_metagem_b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Burning Shadowspirit Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Red Socket - <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52257/brilliant-chimeras-eye">
<img alt="Brilliant Chimera's Eye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Chimera's Eye</span></a> &gt; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52207/brilliant-inferno-ruby">
<img alt="Brilliant Inferno Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior6.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brilliant Inferno Ruby</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Blue Socket - <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52217/veiled-demonseye">
<img alt="Veiled Demonseye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Veiled Demonseye</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Yellow Socket - <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52208/reckless-ember-topaz">
<img alt="Reckless Ember Topaz" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cutgemsuperior4.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reckless Ember Topaz</span></a></div></li></ul>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-arrow-right">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Check the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/classes/warlock/destruction/dps-enchants-gems-pve">
<b>Destruction Warlock DPS Enchants and Gems</b></a> guide for more details on Destruction <a class="icontiny c9" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=9/warlock">
<img alt="Warlock" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warlock.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warlock</span></a> Enchants and Gems.</div></li></ul>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="reforging">Reforging</h4>Reforging is a system introduced in Cataclysm that allows you to convert 40% of one secondary stat or spirit on an item into another secondary stat or spirit. It can be used on any item with an item level of 200 or higher. You can only reforge one stat per item at a time. We usually convert them into hit rating until we are capped. After which we can use reforging to meet our most realistic "soft haste cap" at which point our damage over time abilities get an extra tick of damage. After that our priority is crit rating.<div class="quote-box" data-has-source="false" data-type="user">
<div class="quote-header"></div>
<div class="quote-body" data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Hit Cap &gt; Realistic Soft Haste Cap &gt; Crit Rating</b></div></div>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-arrow-right">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Check the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/classes/warlock/destruction/dps-stat-priority-attributes-pve">
<b>Destruction Warlock DPS Stat Priority and Attributes</b></a> guide for more details on Destruction <a class="icontiny c9" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=9/warlock">
<img alt="Warlock" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warlock.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warlock</span></a> Stat Priority and Attributes.</div></li></ul>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="realistic-pre-raid-best-in-slot-example">
<div class="wh-center" style="text-align: -webkit-center;">Realistic Pre-Raid Best in Slot Example</div></h5>Note this example has a lot of crafted or bought items. Most of these can be replaced with either <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a> or <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> items. <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> items have been left out of the embed due to the time restraint required to get them outside raiding.<br/>
<br/>
