<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Warlock DPS in Pre-Raid</h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="head">Head</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60237/crown-of-the-twilight-queen">
<img alt="Crown of the Twilight Queen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_robe_raidmage_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crown of the Twilight Queen</span></a> is overall the strongest head item we can get before entering raids, it does cost 80 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a> which is rewarded from doing Heroics on the Inferno Protocol difficulty. Getting enough hit rating is often the main challenge in pre-raid gear. This is because of the limited amount of stats on lower item-lever gear. <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=202/engineering">
<img alt="Engineering" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> provides the best option in the form of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59449/lightweight-bio-optic-killshades">
<img alt="Lightweight Bio-Optic Killshades" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_newgoggles.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightweight Bio-Optic Killshades</span></a> in which we can choose which secondary stat we get through Cogwheels. Ideally, we would put in <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59493/rigid-cogwheel">
<img alt="Rigid Cogwheel" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid Cogwheel</span></a> for the massive hit rating that it provides. Another alternative for those without <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=202/engineering">
<img alt="Engineering" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Engineering</span></a> is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69577/collar-of-bones">
<img alt="Collar of Bones" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_102.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Collar of Bones</span></a> which drops from <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=23863/daakara">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Daakara</span></a> in <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=3805/zulaman">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Zul'Aman</span></a>. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60249/shadowflame-hood">
<img alt="Shadowflame Hood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_cloth_raidwarlock_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shadowflame Hood</span></a> is also a good option that can be bought with 32 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>, note that the 4-piece set bonus is not majorly important for Warlocks and you probably save your <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a> for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60237/crown-of-the-twilight-queen">
<img alt="Crown of the Twilight Queen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_robe_raidmage_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crown of the Twilight Queen</span></a> instead.<div class="box" data-level="null">
<b>Head Enchant</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86932/arcanum-of-hyjal">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_masterofelements.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of Hyjal</span></a></div>
